# Arena game authoring

When changing [`examples/arenaGameApp/main.silc`](examples/arenaGameApp/main.silc):

1. **Do not hand-edit** the scene tree. Use `silc assist "<task>" examples/arenaGameApp/main.silc` (or the equivalent from that directory).
2. After assist writes the file, validate with `silc build examples/arenaGameApp/main.silc` (and run if needed).
3. Runtime / pixel / kernel fixes belong in `crates/sil-codegen/templates/game/` (and related lower/catalog code), not in hand-patched `.silc`.

When assist produces invalid or snow-era shapes (terrain, wake, controls, mixed `app`+`game`):

- Fix **`silc assist`** in `crates/sil-rlm` (author prompts, `task_pattern`, `is_game_shaped`, preservation/purity checks, corpus) and game catalog docs as needed.
- Then re-run assist against `main.silc` — do not bypass with a manual patch unless assist is blocked and you are only unblocking tooling.
